# AG-3 Safe Ransomware Simulation and Recovery Validation

## 1. Overview

This document records the safe ransomware simulation and recovery validation completed for the AG-3 Cyber Resilience project.

The purpose of this test was to demonstrate how the proposed environment can:

- Detect suspicious file changes using Wazuh.
- Identify ransomware-like file behaviour in the Nextcloud environment.
- Generate a high-severity security alert.
- Recover affected files from a protected Restic backup stored on MinIO.
- Return the Nextcloud test folder to its normal operational state.

No real ransomware or malicious encryption was used during this test. The ransomware impact was safely simulated by renaming selected test files with a `.locked` extension and creating a simulated ransom note.

---

## 2. Test Environment

The following AG-3 systems were involved in the validation:

| Component | Role | IP Address |
|---|---|---|
| APP01 | Ubuntu Server, Nextcloud, Restic and Wazuh Agent | `10.20.20.10` |
| MON01 | Wazuh Manager and monitoring platform | `10.20.30.10` |
| BKP01 | MinIO backup storage | `10.20.40.10` |
| pfSense | Firewall and network segmentation | `10.20.20.1` on VLAN 20 |

The ransomware simulation was restricted to the following Nextcloud test directory:

```text
/var/ncdata/manager/files/Ransomeware-Demo
```

This isolated test folder was used so that the simulation would not affect other Nextcloud data.

