## 5. Wazuh File Integrity Monitoring

Wazuh File Integrity Monitoring (FIM) was configured on APP01 to monitor the ransomware demonstration directory.

The following directory configuration was added to the existing `<syscheck>` section of the Wazuh agent configuration:

```xml
<directories realtime="yes" check_all="yes">/var/ncdata/manager/files/Ransomeware-Demo</directories>
```

This allowed Wazuh to monitor changes to the test files in realtime.

A normal FIM test confirmed that Wazuh was able to identify new files in the directory.

For example, creation of:

```text
FIM-TEST-2.txt
```

generated the following Wazuh event:

```text
Rule ID: 554
Description: File added to the system.
Mode: realtime
```

This confirmed that APP01 was successfully sending realtime FIM events to MON01.

---

## 6. Custom Ransomware Detection Rules

Custom Wazuh rules were created on MON01 to identify the specific ransomware indicators used during the controlled simulation.

Two rule IDs were allocated:

- `100110` – Detection of files with the `.locked` extension.
- `100111` – Detection of the simulated ransom note.

The custom rules were configured in:

```text
/var/ossec/etc/rules/local_rules.xml
```

The following rules were added:

```xml
<group name="ag3,ransomware,syscheck,">

  <rule id="100110" level="12">
    <if_group>syscheck</if_group>
    <field name="file" type="pcre2">Ransomeware-Demo/.*\.locked$</field>
    <description>AG3 possible ransomware activity - locked file detected in Nextcloud test folder: $(file)</description>
    <group>ransomware_detection,file_integrity,</group>
  </rule>

  <rule id="100111" level="14">
    <if_group>syscheck</if_group>
    <field name="file" type="pcre2">Ransomeware-Demo/README_RECOVERY_TEST\.txt$</field>
    <description>AG3 ransomware simulation detected - ransom note created in Nextcloud test folder: $(file)</description>
    <group>ransomware_detection,ransom_note,file_integrity,</group>
  </rule>

</group>
```

These rules provided higher-severity alerts when ransomware-like indicators appeared inside the controlled test folder.

