## 7. Safe Ransomware Simulation

A dedicated script was created to make the ransomware simulation simple and repeatable.

Script location:

```text
/usr/local/sbin/ag3-ransomware-demo
```

The simulation was started using:

```bash
sudo ag3-ransomware-demo
```

The script performed the following controlled actions:

1. Confirmed that the test directory existed.
2. Checked that the folder was not already in a simulated ransomware state.
3. Renamed the test files by adding the `.locked` extension.
4. Created a simulated ransom note.
5. Updated the Nextcloud file index.

For example:

```text
Finance data.docx
```

became:

```text
Finance data.docx.locked
```

The same process was applied to the other test files.

A harmless simulated ransom note was also created:

```text
README_RECOVERY_TEST.txt
```

The simulation did not perform encryption and did not execute any real ransomware or malicious software.

